s genders and sexualities than the original was). Do you guys see this too or am I imagining things?<br /> <br /> Also shouldn\u2019t it be Le Salon des Femmes Nouvelles? Femmes is a feminine noun in French.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T07:50:54-07:00","id":1442971,"title":"","content":"I think that was to idea for the entire Trinity Continuum. The 90s were very pessimistic and nowadays we need more optimistic views.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T08:03:59-07:00","id":1442975,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. I think I can work with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T09:22:47-07:00","id":1442979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1442962#post1442962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1e version seems somehow darker tone, more tragic and mournful for a lost past.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not something I ever got out of the 1e rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T10:07:39-07:00","id":1442989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1442979#post1442979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not something I ever got out of the 1e rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>The death of Annabelle and Michael\u2019s grief afterward as being the end of an era. OTOH you are one of the writers so I trust your judgment on this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T11:33:34-07:00","id":1442994,"title":"","content":"We need more optimism in our games - especially, when you can punch Nazis in it. In Poland, our modern, real world government is having quasi-fascists leanings, so fighting Nazis would be great substitute for our government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-08-2021, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T14:25:28-07:00","id":1443019,"title":"","content":"Okay. But there weren\u2019t any Nazis in the 1930s (I mean, there were, but no one was at war with them except the countries they invaded). That was the 1940s. 1930s was like Doc Savage and the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T14:46:06-07:00","id":1443027,"title":"","content":"The Nazis were around and murdering people in the late 1920s. Before them groups called Freikorps (pardon my total lack of spelling skills in any language) were butchering people from the end of WWI on through to the formation of the Storm Troopers which most of them joined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T15:10:16-07:00","id":1443032,"title":"","content":"The Nazis were, unfortunately, well-considered internationally in the 30s (Hitler himself appeared on Times Magazine as 'Man of the Year'). In that more racist age, even being openly anti-semitic and anti-minorities was not bad to a considerable part of western society. Mind you, people that had more modern sensibilities or dealt with them had a good idea they were bad news. None more than Maxwell Mercer, who would certainly have a vision of their true stripes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T15:55:08-07:00","id":1443042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443019#post1443019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. But there weren\u2019t any Nazis in the 1930s (I mean, there were, but no one was at war with them except the countries they invaded). That was the 1940s. 1930s was like Doc Savage and the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>you know the Indiana Jones movies are set in the 30s, right? The fact that there weren\u2019t armies fighting yet, doesn\u2019t mean the Third Reich* doesn\u2019t have agents at work in the world to punch if that\u2019s the story a table wants to do.<br /> <br /> also don\u2019t forget the Spanish Civil War<br /> <br /> *Hitler came to power in 33","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T15:58:55-07:00","id":1443044,"title":"","content":"The ascension of the Nazis to the power in Germany start in the 20s (Hitler\u2019s Mein Kamph was published in the 20s, and he already had a good amount of followers).<br /> They took control of the National Social party (that become the Nazi name) and build their representation in the parliament, to the point they named Hitler the Chanceler in 1933, when they start to officially hunting people they didn\u2019t consider proper Germans (not only Jews, but some Christian groups too, gays, not to mention the non-white). Before that they were doing it illegally or at least non officially.<br /> They start \u201ctaking back\u201d what they called Germany (as described in their national anthem, by the way), including Austria, Belgium, Denmark, Poland, etc.<br /> As they were not attacking the western countries so far, and controlling the expansion of the soviets and their revolutions in Eastern Europe, England and France did nothing, and kept that way until the Germans broke to pact with USSR about Poland, starting officially the war.<br /> They went all the way to the end of Poland and than turned around and took France, when England joined USSR against Germany in 1939.<br /> <br /> So in 1934, Hittler was the big boss in Germany (not sure if called Chanceler or already Fuher), the German army was all around the world (Africa, Asia, Middle East and Europe) and recruiting locals (only particularly white people, of course) to the SS. I think they had already took Austria and some other countries (most of them still trying to recover from the destruction of WWI).<br /> <br /> That is a very bad resume of the time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T16:49:01-07:00","id":1443048,"title":"","content":"1933: Hitler becomes Chancellor, passes the Enabling Act which begins the process of converting the Weimar Republic into the single-party Nazi Germany.<br /> 1934: <b>Trinity Continuum: Adventure!</b><br /> 1936: <i>Raiders of the Lost Ark</i>. Indiana Jones fights Nazis.<br /> 1938: <i>Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade</i>. Indiana Jones fights Nazis (again). <i>The Rocketeer</i>. Cliff Secord keeps a powerful invention away from Nazis.<br /> 1939: World War II begins.<br /> <br /> Lots of room in there for Nazi-punching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T17:48:48-07:00","id":1443056,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t know all that. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T18:18:37-07:00","id":1443059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443048#post1443048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1933: Hitler becomes Chancellor, passes the Enabling Act which begins the process of converting the Weimar Republic into the single-party Nazi Germany.<br /> 1934: <b>Trinity Continuum: Adventure!</b><br /> 1936: <i>Raiders of the Lost Ark</i>. Indiana Jones fights Nazis.<br /> 1938: <i>Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade</i>. Indiana Jones fights Nazis (again). <i>The Rocketeer</i>. Cliff Secord keeps a powerful invention away from Nazis.<br /> 1939: World War II begins.<br /> <br /> Lots of room in there for Nazi-punching.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d also add \u201cHitler sends Nazi forces to fight for Fascist victory in Spanish Civil War\u201d to \u201836, which seems like a particularly ripe lynch pin for Inspired to alter the direction of.<br /> <br /> of course stopping Stalin\u2019s agents from turning a Republican victory into a ML party dictatorship against the will of most the Spanish heroes he was aiding will represent its own challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-07-2021, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T07:31:55-07:00","id":1443118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1442848#post1442848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new Allegiances are pretty interesting. Good job, devs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah; I get that a Path for Invictus Umbra might be redundant if Les Fantomes from the corebook are a player faction (and probably originated as people disgusted with the more selfish direction it took), but I really appreciated how clear it is that it's a good idea that was hijacked by more selfish interests and an unwillingness to call itself out, not always hypocritical. The REG is wonderfully creepy, and the Contendorri are very useful all-purpose goons who nonetheless have a grander expression that makes them possible chronicle villains, and respectable enough to be friendly rivals at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T09:13:44-07:00","id":1443126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443044#post1443044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ascension of the Nazis to the power in Germany start in the 20s (Hitler\u2019s Mein Kamph was published in the 20s, and he already had a good amount of followers).<br /> They took control of the National Social party (that become the Nazi name) and build their representation in the parliament, to the point they named Hitler the Chanceler in 1933, when they start to officially hunting people they didn\u2019t consider proper Germans (not only Jews, but some Christian groups too, gays, not to mention the non-white). Before that they were doing it illegally or at least non officially.<br /> They start \u201ctaking back\u201d what they called Germany (as described in their national anthem, by the way), including Austria, Belgium, Denmark, Poland, etc.<br /> As they were not attacking the western countries so far, and controlling the expansion of the soviets and their revolutions in Eastern Europe, England and France did nothing, and kept that way until the Germans broke to pact with USSR about Poland, starting officially the war.<br /> They went all the way to the end of Poland and than turned around and took France, when England joined USSR against Germany in 1939.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. The pact with Stalin facilitated the invasion of Poland. It was a violation of the line in the sand Britain and France had drawn over his expansion (after years of acquiescing). The USSR wasn\u2019t in the war until Hitler broke their no aggression pact by invading them in \u201841 starting a second front in an ongoing war, possibly one of the most inexplicably stupid mistakes in world history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in 1934, Hittler was the big boss in Germany (not sure if called Chanceler or already Fuher), </div> </div> </div>He becomes Fuher when President von Hindenburg dies in August of 34, and he combines the office of President with the Chancellorship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-08-2021, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T09:56:27-07:00","id":1443134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443126#post1443126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite. The pact with Stalin facilitated the invasion of Poland. It was a violation of the line in the sand Britain and France had drawn over his expansion (after years of acquiescing). The USSR wasn\u2019t in the war until Hitler broke their no aggression pact by invading them in \u201841 starting a second front in an ongoing war, possibly one of the most inexplicably stupid mistakes in world history.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He becomes Fuher when President von Hindenburg dies in August of 34, and he combines the office of President with the Chancellorship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the corrections. It\u2019s been years since I studied WWII and I was remembering wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T15:45:11-07:00","id":1443300,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking of the moment of Inspiration and how it can be played with. Like imagine if at the moment one becomes Inspired they are whisked away by the energy to some other place or time, do an adventure there, and then come back to the world a second later empowered. Or as Inspiration strikes they get a vision of somewhere else, or something else, good or bad, that helps to motivate them and stuff. <br /> <br /> It could be a quite interesting flux event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T18:27:33-07:00","id":1443314,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a bit Mage the Awakening crossing with Tron... something that may be really interesting to play.<br /> <br /> it can also you suddenly connect to tour other selves from other realities and gain some of their memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T18:56:11-07:00","id":1443319,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of seeing multiple visions of similar 'you' in other worlds and places and times. It could be an interesting focal point of trying to either make this world NOT like the other one or actually like the other one. Like in one vision they see their world torn apart in an endless war (and since this is the pulp era I would figure Nazi's are the endless fighting force) or they can see a world of high technology where power is beamed and zepplins fly between massive art deco buildings (Tesla empowered). Maybe they see an image of a world covered in jungles and forests and them making a miraculous find (a lost world sort of image, maybe a return of Atlantis or something else). Then the character's find themselves back in the real present, now inspired. <br /> <br /> Or even, and this would only work for certain campaigns, imagine a prologue where the players are handed a micro-character sheet with some high level abilities in a doomsday senario. The moment the final player dies the image snaps to the present, where they were normal people doing normal things in a normal world. Of course, said normal-life is now behind them as their vision has brought about their inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T17:01:06-07:00","id":1443674,"title":"","content":"Ok, I tried, I really did, but I can't really figure it out on my own. What does the Big Boss edge actually do? Every time I read it's description, I just keep thinking &quot;isn't this just a path invocation? With an extra drawback?&quot;<br /> Yes, yes, you are 'in charge', but what does that mean? Or to put it another way, what difference does that make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T11:13:23-07:00","id":1443764,"title":"","content":"So, from the new section: <br /> <br /> All of the Inspired get access to Dramatic Editing; but for stalwarts and mesmerists, the costs are increased by one. It's not specifically stated that this cost bump is just for stalwarts and mesmerists; but it <i>is</i> stated that the cost bump doesn't apply to the subsequent sections. And the very next section is\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026that daredevils get a cost <i>break</i> for Dramatic Editing, <i>reducing</i> the cost by one. They also get to spend Momentum instead of Inspiration on Dramatic Editing if they wish. <br /> <br /> Mesmerists get to \u201cdramatically edit\u201d <i>which Psychic Gifts</i> they have access to, spending Inspiration or Momentum to substitute one Gift for another for the rest of the scene. Okay; I can <i>kind of</i> see that as Dramatic Editing. <br /> <br /> Stalwarts get to spend Inspiration or Momentum to treat one or all of their Facets as maxed out. Doing it for all Facets causes burnout. <br /> <br /> And all types get to spend Inspiration to use their Gifts in creative ways (that is, to do things that aren't technically in the Gift's write-up), with the cost being set by just how much of a stretch the creative use is. <br /> <br /> Also, each type of Inspired get a special means of recovering Inspiration once per session that's tied to one of the Facets: daredevils use Boldness and the Intuitive Facet; mesmerists use Concentration and the Reflective Facet; and stalwarts use Telluric Catalyst and the Destructive Facet. <br /> <br /> The stalwart-specific tweaks to Inspiration and Dramatic Editing involve a new Condition called Telluric Burnout, which is a precursor to the Transformations of the Aberrant era. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Overall, I like these additions. That said, I'm going to house-rule it slightly for my games: I'm going to revise that first bit as \u201c<i>anyone</i> can engage in Dramatic Editing, whether or not they're Inspired. The cost is double that given in the core book, and must be paid in Momentum.\u201d I'll keep the rest the same: daredevils get a price break; mesmerists get to substitute Gifts; stalwarts get to exceed their limits; all of them can use their Gifts creatively; and the various types of Inspired get to use their choice of Inspiration or Momentum to pay for their Dramatic Editing specialties. <br /> <br /> The reason for this tweak is that I like the original <b>Adventure!</b> concept of Dramatic Editing as a metagame concept, and this allows that concept to coexist with daredevils as reality warpers. It also makes it easier to port these rules over to other eras: novas and psiads and superiors and psions don't have Inspiration; but with this tweak, they can still spend Momentum on Dramatic Editing, as can baselines. Likewise, Talents become a bit more effective in eras where psychics and/or superhumans are running around: it's mentioned that the cost break for daredevils comes from the ambient Telluric Energies in the wake of the Hammersmith Event, and a similar rationale would apply in Aberrant and \u00c6on (though not in the core book's setting or in Anima).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T12:22:32-07:00","id":1443782,"title":"","content":"1e Daredevil was not necessarily powered, or reality bending, and that is really important in the way the game flows. We treat them as powered by reality bending, but even in game they are not sure how it works, even the most fantastic people in the world can\u2019t pinpoint when they are using powers or just lucky.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Editing (changing small things, or big ones) is a good metagaming, I mean, you take control of the game from the GM, it\u2019s very metagaming. If it is ok to Stalwarts and Mesmerists to use Dramatic Editing, I would say non-inspired characters could do the same.<br /> <br /> Now, the other uses of inspiration should apply only to inspired (some require facet values), and that is what I think is the most superhuman aspect of the Talents/Daredevils (at least measurable in game). That must be available to all inspired that are based in Inspiration and only to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T12:37:28-07:00","id":1443786,"title":"","content":"So the Gifts chapter came out and I have to say I am really liking it. The Daredevils are as cool as the Talents that we already know, and thus fit well. Stalwart powers are brilliant and I like the nature of them. Mesmerist powers are intriguing to me, though I am more in the Stalwart frame right now and thus its that where my focus really is. <br /> <br /> Its funny to me that in the previous edition there were some Mesmerist powers that I really wanted to be Stalwart powers but in this edition there really isn't. There is one or two that I think would fit (the memory palace one for example, that and some telluric sensory powers) but for the most part Stalwart is Stalwart and Mesmerist is Mesmerist. <br /> <br /> I will state that this is a pdf that I will be keeping open so that I can over the powers in more detail, for I really like the nature of what they can do. So much potential. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> One thing I don't see, and would really like for there to be a sidebar about, is the longevity of the Inspired. I totally can see Stalwarts and Mesmerists (and maybe certain rare Daredevils) getting something that makes them immortal. I don't think this should be a direct Gift as its sort of useless in normal play but something like &quot;if trait x reaches y then you are immortal&quot; or even &quot;if you have x gifts your telluric pattern is strong enough to stand up to eternity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T13:00:15-07:00","id":1443793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443786#post1443786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Gifts chapter came out and I have to say I am really liking it. The Daredevils are as cool as the Talents that we already know, and thus fit well. Stalwart powers are brilliant and I like the nature of them. Mesmerist powers are intriguing to me, though I am more in the Stalwart frame right now and thus its that where my focus really is.<br /> <br /> Its funny to me that in the previous edition there were some Mesmerist powers that I really wanted to be Stalwart powers but in this edition there really isn't. There is one or two that I think would fit (the memory palace one for example, that and some telluric sensory powers) but for the most part Stalwart is Stalwart and Mesmerist is Mesmerist.<br /> <br /> I will state that this is a pdf that I will be keeping open so that I can over the powers in more detail, for I really like the nature of what they can do. So much potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with you about Stalwart powers, the way they are working now are just great, and they made it better than 1e. To describe Doc Primoris you don\u2019t need to pick some psychic gifts and make them dynamic, for example.<br /> <br /> Another thing I like in the Stalwart gifts is the way they where broken in Attribute and Power gifts, it makes much easier to say \u201cfor reasons of genre, no power gift will be available\u201d.<br /> <br /> On the Mesmerist side, I was expecting Biological gifts being exclusively BK and VK related, but actually they are \u201call that is related to biology\u201d, what means you can use some of the Telepathy and Clair powers (among others) as biological because they affect biological aspects, like talking to animals is a Telepathy power (a little aspect of a mode dot), or sensing a target by touching a former part of their body is a clairsentience power, but as both deal with biological aspects of reality they are biological. Honestly it put the borders between different kinds of powers in a grey area, but it\u2019s a personal point of view. It\u2019s also irrelevant because it has effects only in the character creation, and further evolution takes no advantage of the original focus (what is good in my opinion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T13:06:16-07:00","id":1443794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443782#post1443782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e Daredevil was not necessarily powered, or reality bending, and that is really important in the way the game flows. We treat them as powered by reality bending, but even in game they are not sure how it works, even the most fantastic people in the world can\u2019t pinpoint when they are using powers or just lucky.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Editing (changing small things, or big ones) is a good metagaming, I mean, you take control of the game from the GM, it\u2019s very metagaming. If it is ok to Stalwarts and Mesmerists to use Dramatic Editing, I would say non-inspired characters could do the same.<br /> <br /> Now, the other uses of inspiration should apply only to inspired (some require facet values), and that is what I think is the most superhuman aspect of the Talents/Daredevils (at least measurable in game). That must be available to all inspired that are based in Inspiration and only to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Things like Gifts and the boosts you can get from Facets should be (and are) unique to the Inspired. The <i>only</i> thing my house rule is intended to change is the access to Dramatic Editing as defined in the TC core book. It's a small change, but has dramatic implications. Everything else they've done, including making Dramatic Editing <i>even easier</i> for daredevils, I intend to use as written.<br /> <br /> Conversely: without that tweak, it's harder to argue that stalwarts and mesmerists <i>aren't</i> the Talent equivalent of QKs: they have access to Dramatic Editing, like daredevils do; and no one else does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-13-2021, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T13:18:25-07:00","id":1443796,"title":"","content":"I also like the additions they've made to Super-Science: among other things, they introduce the notion of there being different traditions of Super-Science. As written, that's primarily there to introduce the idea that you can use the Super-Science rules to represent stuff that's more traditionally thought of as magical (\u201cArtifacts of Enigmatic Power\u201d); but I could also see it letting you deal in more bizarre or divergent sciences as well. Then there's \u201cMoments of Desperate Genius\u201d, which is more of the McGuyver thing of jury rigging your Super-Science to do something it wasn't designed to; basically, a Super-Science counterpart to the new Dramatic Editing option of improvising alternate uses for your Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T14:03:08-07:00","id":1443801,"title":"","content":"The one thing I do have to say, and I commented about this on the kickstarter itself, is that I am not sure if all the placement of Stalwart Gifts (almost said Knacks, lol) are connected to the right Attribute. They seem to have the sense powers as Composure, which I am not sure works. (I didn't post this in the feedback form because I am not sure if they have a reason for it. I wish to err on the side that they have a reason. I am doing this because the Gifts themselves are brilliant.) <br /> <br /> Oh. As a note. I totally see the potential for Doctor Primoris to have his 'plasma' powers that in the previous edition were represented by him having some Mesmerist Knacks. Here he probably has the fire blast and the fire sensing and the fire other things power. <br /> <br /> I also really like the whole push one's powers into slightly off the standard path ability they have. Its such a cool element. Very thematic too. I mean in-game one session sees them pushing a power into a slightly different direction, things are successful, leading them to buying a related Gift the next time they get the XP. <br /> <br /> Lots of good stuff here. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I do think, as a note, that Stalwart based healing another powers should exist. Maybe its not as much as the whole Mesmerist element but there are ways that a Stalwart should be able to do that in a way that is better than mundanes. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I love this chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:22:35-07:00","id":1443837,"title":"","content":"Is there any force/threat/etc keeping the overt powers of Stalwarts and Mesmerists secret in the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:46:15-07:00","id":1443840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443837#post1443837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any force/threat/etc keeping the overt powers of Stalwarts and Mesmerists secret in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>( Joke ) <a href=\"https://marvel.fandom.com/wiki/Terrigen_Mist\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Terrigen</span></span></span> Mists</b></a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T23:32:39-07:00","id":1443852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443837#post1443837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any force/threat/etc keeping the overt powers of Stalwarts and Mesmerists secret in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. In that regard, it's no different than Aberrant or \u00c6on. Adventure! is not a \u201csecret magic\u201d setting; and the Inspired do not operate behind a masquerade. To the extent that the world <i>isn't</i> radically altered by them, it's because of a combination of comparatively lower power levels, fewer Inspired, and the Inspired being curious types who are frequently off somewhere investigating a strange place rather than wandering around downtown Manhattan. <br /> <br /> But they <i>do</i> make their way into the newspapers, and the public <i>does</i> follow their adventures. And a hundred years later, they have <i>not</i> been forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T05:13:23-07:00","id":1443865,"title":"","content":"Two things<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thanks for explaining. I\u2019ve only read Adventure! 1e, a couple old Aberrant books and a little of the old Trinity core book (the one that got renamed Aeon in the reboot), so I wasn\u2019t sure just how secret the Inspired and their adventures were. That clarifies things.<br /> <br /> Also I noticed they didn\u2019t update the old Sex Symbol stalwart gift from 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T06:07:16-07:00","id":1443866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443852#post1443852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. In that regard, it's no different than Aberrant or \u00c6on. Adventure! is not a \u201csecret magic\u201d setting; and the Inspired do not operate behind a masquerade. To the extent that the world <i>isn't</i> radically altered by them, it's because of a combination of comparatively lower power levels, fewer Inspired, and the Inspired being curious types who are frequently off somewhere investigating a strange place rather than wandering around downtown Manhattan. <br /> <br /> But they <i>do</i> make their way into the newspapers, and the public <i>does</i> follow their adventures. And a hundred years later, they have <i>not</i> been forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m just asking because in the canon timeline the general public seems unaware superpowers exist before N-Day","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T06:22:26-07:00","id":1443869,"title":"","content":"The thing that shaped peoples' reaction to N-Day was less a matter of \u201cwait: superpowers are real?\u201d and more a matter of shock and awe: how <i>many</i> Novas came crawling out of the woodworks all at once, and how powerful they were. Especially the latter. As impressive as stalwarts are, they're not gods striding the Earth; Novas <i>are</i>. (Not literally, of course; that's Scion's domain. But figuratively.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:15:36-07:00","id":1443884,"title":"","content":"I think the issue with Stalwarts and Mesmerists not being know by the public before N-Day is the highest population of Inspired had happened 100-80 years prior, and probably peaked in the thousands. Most of them had no visible super powers, working more subtly, and avoiding the spotlight to avoid become a lab rat. After some years they become urban legends, or people believe the stories were overwhelmed by newspapers and gossip circles.<br /> <br /> After Hammersmith effect faded away, the inspired population probably peaked in the few hundreds around the world, most of them hiding from Branch 9, or being supported by Aeon and other Allegiances. Must remember the description of some allegiances in core say the powered people were studied and in the post WWII word it means being opens and have the organs being observed...<br /> <br /> With N-Day the numbers and the power level was too high to hide (in Aberrant they even say some novas were hiding even after N-Day) and so the public become aware very fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:46:21-07:00","id":1443888,"title":"","content":"Communication was less straightforward in Adventure!: radio communication was still fairly new, Morse code was still the primary choice for long-distance communication at speed. A lot of news was distributed via newsreels in theatres, but that would require cameras at the location: you send a camera crew to where a thing (like the War) is already happening.<br /> <br /> If a newspaper wanted to report on something, they needed to send their own reporters and cameramen, or else make something up.<br /> <br /> And many newspapers did exactly that. They made things up to sell copies. Both to attract readers and to compete with other periodicals. In some cases, newspapers were little better than sensationalist tabloids.<br /> <br /> So if a newspaper reports on a woman who can lift a car, or a man with a jet-pack... well those stories may be accurate, and people might believe them at the time. But as the era progresses, international communication improves at about the same rate that Inspired phenomena drop off, so it's easy for future people to look at the outrageous of the 20s at 30s and dismiss them as sensationalist reporting. There's no proof, and besides, everyone <i>knows</i> that intelligent gorillas are the domain of fiction.<br /> <br /> So by the time the Nova Age rolls around, there are few people who still remember or believe anything about the Adventure! era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:56:42-07:00","id":1443891,"title":"","content":"&quot;Back in my youth my neighbor lifted a whole car on her back,&quot; says a man to his son. &quot;Sure pops, sure,&quot; the son says in response to what he perceived as the ramblings of an old man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},