e anything about the Adventure! era.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you so much for this answer. It's a simple explanation that makes total sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T13:53:13-07:00","id":1443930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443891#post1443891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Back in my youth my neighbor lifted a whole car on her back,&amp;quot; says a man to his son. &amp;quot;Sure pops, sure,&amp;quot; the son says in response to what he perceived as the ramblings of an old man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T15:13:44-07:00","id":1443944,"title":"","content":"&quot;he was wearing a red and blue circus outfit.\u201d <br /> <br /> EDIT: I think I may have been too subtle. I was making a reference to Action Comics #1, which is public domain now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-15-2021, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T18:30:59-07:00","id":1443964,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking about areas that I think Stalwarts need to cover and one such thing is a Gift that reduces sleep needs, probably with some bonus or something to make it a worthwhile Gift. (If this is in already my bad, I had an annoying distraction interrupt my reading called work.)<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On another note I am not entirely sure I like those Gifts that have a disadvantage built in. (A perfect example being Hyper-perceptivity.) To me powers should be a positive thing not something with a drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 04-14-2021, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T21:12:43-07:00","id":1443976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443964#post1443964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was thinking about areas that I think Stalwarts need to cover and one such thing is a Gift that reduces sleep needs, probably with some bonus or something to make it a worthwhile Gift. (If this is in already my bad, I had an annoying distraction interrupt my reading called work.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 61: Beyond the Human Limit. You don't need to sleep for a week, among other benefits.<br /> <br /> I find the mesmerist Gift Traversing the Impassable (page 84) rather odd, since the only psion effect I can picture as giving a comparable benefit is quantakinesis (transmutation) + biokinesis (to affect yourself), even though quantakinesis isn't going to be unlocked for about 200 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T05:52:47-07:00","id":1444024,"title":"","content":"Finally looking through the new gifts. Looks like Daredevils do a lot of giving themselves conditions. That should make them pretty good Momentum generators, which should feed their Dramatic Editing nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T06:00:22-07:00","id":1444025,"title":"","content":"I also like the Celestial Goddess Inspired artifact. Maybe it\u2019s like a foreshadowing of Aegis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T06:38:33-07:00","id":1444030,"title":"","content":"Traversing the Impassable is more related to Teleportation (sometimes Biokinesis) in other games that deal with Psionics, but you can\u2019t do it with any of the 3 modes (or 6, adding BK). It\u2019s not the only one that have this feeling of non connection to the modes.<br /> <br /> I think the conditions and complications related to Daredevil gifts are awesome. They create not only momentum, but also that feeling of \u201cgot lucky\u201d in many situations, just great.<br /> <br /> Celestial Goddess is the best reference to Aegis so far. I tried to find another reference to some pulp goddess, like Ayeisha ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayesha_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayesha_(novel)</a> ), but can\u2019t find any of them using weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T09:19:30-07:00","id":1444039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1443944#post1443944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;he was wearing a red and blue circus outfit.\u201d<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think I may have been too subtle. I was making a reference to Action Comics #1, which is public domain now.</div> </div> </div> </div>not till 2034 in the US thanks to the last Disney pushed extension","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T14:42:25-07:00","id":1444069,"title":"","content":"Signed up today. <br /> <br /> Now, I think a &quot;Mindspeech&quot; gift is needed. You might suggest that it's more suited to science fantasy settings. <br /> <br /> In fact there should be a table in the book which offers a list of genres and a chart of which gifts fit which genre. Neither Ming the Merciless nor Rema the Bird Girl belong in a hard boiled detective story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:03:14-07:00","id":1444082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstar