d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T00:49:02-07:00","id":1444459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444449#post1444449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want it so bad it hurts! God so many setting ideas</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have lost my cool for a moment, but the story fuel from the pathing of the accidental time traveller is so very tempting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T07:44:06-07:00","id":1444501,"title":"","content":"When it comes to powers I totally would like to see what areas Superiors/Novas have that Stalwarts miss - the same for Mesmerists and Psiads. Then I would like to think on why that may be, if leaving the area blank makes sense, or what needs to be done to fill it in if Stalwarts should get that sort of power. To me a really good view of things are the Mega-Edges, which in many ways are very similar to the Gifts of the Stalwarts. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> On the stretch goal, I very much would love to see the alternate timelines and settings book. The potential for some great fun on that is amazing.<br /> <br /> I also have to say that I hope one version has a world that has public access to other worlds, dimensions, realities. That would be a cool game.<br /> <br /> The one thing I do have to say is that while it is quite logical to see how Stalwart Doctor Primoris can go to Nova Divis Mal and Mesmerist Sara can go to Psion the whole temporal element of Mercer is not really visible in the Daredevil/Talent power suite. Leading to him being a bit of an unconnected oddity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 04-18-2021, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T15:40:50-07:00","id":1444557,"title":"","content":"I think that\u2019s because Mercer is unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T16:39:56-07:00","id":1444567,"title":"","content":"Well on Mercer the question for me is why is he any more unique then the one who becomes a nova and the one who becomes a psiad. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying regular Daredevils should have full on time travel Gifts, all I am saying is that maybe some of their published Gifts could lead us to the idea of why their superform goes with time travel and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T17:36:53-07:00","id":1444571,"title":"","content":"Maybe if the talent push their facets beyond 5 or inspiration beyond 10 they can do it. It's a matter of laking the brute power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T19:29:10-07:00","id":1444586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444567#post1444567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well on Mercer the question for me is why is he any more unique then the one who becomes a nova and the one who becomes a psiad. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying regular Daredevils should have full on time travel Gifts, all I am saying is that maybe some of their published Gifts could lead us to the idea of why their superform goes with time travel and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic Editing could be thought of as revising the timeline, at least as done by daredevils. (I definitely prefer recasting the limited access to it that stalwarts and mesmerists get as a genre convention thing rather than an in-game thing; but that's me.) <i>All</i> daredevil Gifts can be described in terms of filtering through possible futures and forcing the one you want to be the one that happens. <br /> <br /> As long as daredevils are not supposed to be seen as superhumans, I don't know what more cam be done to tie them to time. And if you're willing to take that extra step and start presenting them as superhumanly lucky, skilled, and/or determined, then you'll need something like <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/301201/Fists-of-Flux\" target=\"_blank\">Fists of Flux</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T20:30:44-07:00","id":1444593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444586#post1444586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dramatic Editing could be thought of as revising the timeline, at least as done by daredevils. (I definitely prefer recasting the limited access to it that stalwarts and mesmerists get as a genre convention thing rather than an in-game thing; but that's me.) <i>All</i> daredevil Gifts can be described in terms of filtering through possible futures and forcing the one you want to be the one that happens.<br /> <br /> As long as daredevils are not supposed to be seen as superhumans, I don't know what more cam be done to tie them to time. And if you're willing to take that extra step and start presenting them as superhumanly lucky, skilled, and/or determined, then you'll need something like <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/301201/Fists-of-Flux\" target=\"_blank\">Fists of Flux</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I\u2019m leaning toward with regard to why Stalwarts and Mesmerists have Dramatic Editing, at least in the extremely high Flux environment of the Inspiration Age, is that they are divergent evolutions from Talents, hence the Facets and the ability to spend Inspiration for Scale, and Facet enhancement, etc.<br /> <br /> Psiads and Novas are the further divergence that occurs specifically because evolution is selecting for adaptations to a lower Flux environment in later eras, so the similarities to Talents fall away and their unique traits get stronger with later eximorph and psychomorph inspirations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-20-2021, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T04:31:42-07:00","id":1444626,"title":"","content":"Canonically they are not, but if that works for your game, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:52:27-07:00","id":1444636,"title":"","content":"This is an odd situation in that the official rules support glamourweaver's take on it (as pointed out, they have Inspiration, Facets, and access to Dramatic Editing that is otherwise restricted to daredevils), while I prefer the canonical stance that IanWatson just stated but find myself having to house-rule some things to make the mechanics reflect that. <br /> <br /> The simplest change is to make Dramatic Editing available to all player characters and major antagonists (but not extras), whether or not they're Inspired, through Momentum but not Inspiration; this would include stalwarts and mesmerists, and daredevils would remain the only characters who can spend Inspiration on traditional Dramatic Editing while stalwarts and mesmerists would still get their alternatives to it that they can spend their Inspiration on. <br /> <br /> Maybe pair this with a text box explaining that Momentum-based Dramatic Editing is a genre convention thing and not an in-setting phenomenon; though that ought to be obvious just from the fact that <i>Momentum</i> is a metagaming currency and doesn't actually exist in the setting. <br /> <br /> A further change would be to replace the Intuitive/Reflective/Destructive Facets that daredevils have with Biological/Energetic/Cognitive Facets for mesmerists and Forceful/Adaptive/Stoic Facets for stalwarts. Combined with the Momentum-fueled Dramatic Editing change above, this makes it so that \u201cstalwart Inspiration\u201d is effectively a prototype for \u201cQuantum\u201d, and \u201cmesmerist Inspiration\u201d is effectively a prototype for \u201cPsi\u201d; and that \u201cInspiration\u201d is used to reflect the in-setting notion that the distinction between the three hasn't been figured out yet. <br /> <br /> But I can understand the revised Facets thing being too much of a change to be officially adopted; but I would like to propose that the Momentum-based Dramatic Editing thing be officially adopted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-19-2021, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T06:31:54-07:00","id":1444640,"title":"","content":"I think a little too much weight is being placed on mechanical abstraction. The map is not the territory. <i>No one</i> in the Trinity Continuum has Facets, but their character sheets do.<br /> <br /> For the sake of mechanical simplicity and genre conventions, the three Inspired types defined in Adventure! are represented using similar mechanics. That's not intended to indicate that they're all the same thing. Our primary goal is to make a fun game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T06:37:52-07:00","id":1444642,"title":"","content":"I think the simplest solution is actually to assume that Dramatic Editing by stalwarts and mesmerists has less to do with them and more to do with the telluric energies flooding the Earth. There is literally so much of the stuff that dinosaurs and lost cities of technologically advanced apes have appeared in out of the way places. It is easy to assume reality has become so fluid that anyone with the power to manipulate the world on a fundamental level can give it that extra push. This doesn't happen in later eras because the Divis Mal and Dr. Bhurano events were specifically limited to quick bursts of telluric energy subsets, and so didn't result in such profound and lasting telluric saturation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T06:59:02-07:00","id":1444647,"title":"","content":"Also, they were different Sources. Mal's being Quantum and Dr. Bhurano's being sub-quantum/noetic. Mal's probably spurred on the eruptions of people into Novas. I don't know if Bhurano's helped jumpstart psiads the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:06:01-07:00","id":1444648,"title":"","content":"You can read the Facets as Biological/Energetic/Cognitive Facets for mesmerists and Forceful/Adaptive/Stoic Facets for stalwarts (and I think I will), the only problem them is that each gift of their group would trigger a single Facet, while the way it is there are some Biological gifts that use Destructive and others that use Reflective facet. In fact it\u2019s not a bad decision, Psiads and novas are far less versatile than Talents and far more focused too, so a Biological Mesmerist would take a big advantage in being focused in Biological powers leaving the other facets low, fir example.<br /> <br /> The second issue there is the use of Facets by themselves, while I do think the extra enhancements from using facets should be a talent thing. What would use of inspiration using Biological Facet do? What would use of inspiration using Forceful facet do? You could remove it completely, and just let the template specific uses of inspiration be used more often than once a session.<br /> <br /> The Dramatic editing to Stalwarts and Mesmerists should be limited to powering up their gifts/facets. To remove the interpretation of Mesmerists and Stalwarts as variations of talents.<br /> <br /> Well, we could very well use the Nova and Psiad template with a few restrictions, Novas would be T2 and limited Q3 using only 75 XP and Psiads limited to Psi 5. But that would be a bit too complex to manage...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:08:17-07:00","id":1444650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444647#post1444647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they were different Sources. Mal's being Quantum and Dr. Bhurano's being sub-quantum/noetic. Mal's probably spurred on the eruptions of people into Novas. I don't know if Bhurano's helped jumpstart psiads the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>She did. Aeon, p 358<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, this noetic event also had effects that Dr. Bhurano never anticipated. It created many hundreds of new Talents and psiads, and transformed more than 300,000 people into la- tent psions. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:08:37-07:00","id":1444651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444640#post1444640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a little too much weight is being placed on mechanical abstraction. The map is not the territory. <i>No one</i> in the Trinity Continuum has Facets, but their character sheets do.<br /> <br /> For the sake of mechanical simplicity and genre conventions, the three Inspired types defined in Adventure! are represented using similar mechanics. That's not intended to indicate that they're all the same thing. Our primary goal is to make a fun game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that; which is part of why I'm not submitting the Facets thing as a proposed change. The Momentum thing, on the other hand, I <i>would</i> like to see officially adopted. My take on it is that Momentum is very clearly <i>not</i> an in-setting thing; Inspiration, on the other hand, at least sometimes represents telluric energies that clearly do exist in the setting. So Dramatic Editing by way of Momentum likewise is clearly a genre convention rather than an in-setting thing, and neatly explains <i>anyone</i> who has a dramatically significant role in the game being able to make the narrative changes that Dramatic Editing represents. Daredevils, meanwhile, are better at it because in the setting they're subconscious timeline manipulators and get to use telluric energies (Inspiration) to manipulate the timeline to their benefit. <br /> <br /> The overall effect is very similar: everyone gets access to the Dramatic Editing rules, with daredevils getting enhanced access. But the implications of the rules are very different: stalwarts, mesmerists, and others who Dramatically Edit aren't altering the timeline the way daredevils are; they're just taking advantage of the plot contrivances that are so common in the pulps. <br /> <br /> And with all due respect: <i>of course</i> the primary goal should be to make a fun game. That should <i>always</i> be the primary goal, no matter what game you're making. But that's a non sequitur. It's not like these ideas would make the game any less fun. But they <i>would</i> make the game more consistent, which for many of us enhances the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:20:36-07:00","id":1444657,"title":"","content":"I'll ask that the discussion of alternate Facets for stalwarts and mesmerists be moved to another thread; I probably shouldn't have brought them up here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444648#post1444648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dramatic editing to Stalwarts and Mesmerists should be limited to powering up their gifts/facets. To remove the interpretation of Mesmerists and Stalwarts as variations of talents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not in the cards; and I'd be against it even if it was. <b>Adventure!</b> has always been about capturing the essence of the pulps; and in that sense, Adventure-era Dramatic Editing is at least somewhat akin to the similar notion from <b>They Came From\u2026</b>: it's a mechanic to represent a genre convention, not an in-game phenomenon that people notice, measure, and talk about. (Except, in the Trinity Continuum, for the daredevils. <i>They're</i> exercising an in-game ability to alter the timeline when they use Inspiration to Dramatically Edit.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:25:37-07:00","id":1444658,"title":"","content":"This really confuses me, what\u2019s in game and what\u2019s not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:29:53-07:00","id":1444659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444658#post1444658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really confuses me, what\u2019s in game and what\u2019s not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> TC is setup for it to be whatever you want. The books present one world of (nearly?) infinite possibilities. Your game world will probably closely resemble it, but it doesn't have to hew exactly to what the designers envisioned for the books. I personally don't use game rule terms as in-game terms, unless it's something like psychic aptitudes and modes. You're free to, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:39:37-07:00","id":1444661,"title":"","content":"So when it comes to Powers in a game (any game) I look at them as a major representation of what the group that uses said powers can do. I look at them as a mechanical abstraction of in-game abilities. <br /> <br /> So when a game says &quot;character x has flame powers' but in the power chapter I see no flame powers I get confused, there is a disconnect between fluff and mechanics. In such cases I usually go the path of least resistance - since mechanics are stuff harder to change if there are no flame powers in the mechanics then there are no flame powers. <br /> <br /> This leads me to my original point - Mercer is a mega-Daredevil and thus what he can do should be Daredevil stuff turned to 11, not something radically different. I would have expected - just like I see with the mega-nova and the mega-mesmerist - to see some imagery of what he can do in their lesser powers. <br /> <br /> A major reason for this mindset is that I can change setting easy but mechanics change a bit harder. <br /> <br /> I should note that I love Adventure! There is so far nothing about it that has me going &quot;nope!&quot;. Its a really really great game. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> for me this is actually somewhat hard to fully answer. I would say Inspired, Telluric Energy, Mesmerist, Stalwart, Daredevil are all in-game terms. I also think that the nature of the powers of Stalwarts as being based on attributes also is known - not so much 'this power is Strength' and more 'the muscles in my body are enhanced, thus enabling me to run better'. <br /> <br /> When it comes to Aeon and Aberrant - Psi, Quantum, Nova, Psiad, Psion, Aptitude and Modes. <br /> <br /> But this can vary quite a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:46:23-07:00","id":1444662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444658#post1444658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really confuses me, what\u2019s in game and what\u2019s not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's always been <b>Adventure!</b>'s cross to bear. The first edition's rules for Dramatic Editing specifically and explicitly said that they were a metagaming mechanic designed to replicate the lucky breaks and coincidences that were so frequently seen in the source material. The only text even remotely saying otherwise was an in-character piece written by Dr. Primorius where he mused that daredevils have some sort of subconscious ability to manipulate probability; and that could easily have been taken as highlighting his prejudice against \u201cordinary folk\u201d: if you're somehow keeping up with the gods (his analogy for stalwarts), then there must be something godlike about you. <br /> <br /> But some readers took it as an indication that daredevils actually <i>are</i> probability manipulators as Primorius surmised, despite the aforementioned rules explicitly saying otherwise. And when the Trinity Universe was revived as the Trinity Continuum, that view was made the official one. <br /> <br /> Which is why I'm not arguing that a <i>daredevil's</i> Dramatic Editing should be treated as a metagaming mechanic; that ship has long since sailed. But from the core book onward, TC has been very clear that reality warping is strictly the purview of Talents; the psychics and superhumans can't do it. So when TC:A! comes along and grants them access to Dramatic Editing, that poses a bit of a problem. But it's an easily resolved problem; all you have to do is to say that stalwarts and mesmerists who use the Dramatic Editing rules aren't manipulating the timeline: for <i>them</i>, go back to the original game's concept that Dramatic Editing is a metagaming system and not something in the setting. <br /> <br /> That's the reasoning I've been using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-19-2021, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T08:42:20-07:00","id":1444832,"title":"","content":"So there's an assumption going on here that the mechanics are not supporting the fiction, and I think people are getting too caught up in the weeds about mesmerists and stalwarts being proto-versions of later iterations of novas and psions. Mesmerists and stalwarts are INSPIRED characters. They are not novas and psions. Not even &quot;not yet.&quot; They are Inspired just like Talents are. The reason the TC Core says that only Talents get Dramatic Editing is because they are the only Inspired type to make it out of the Inspired Age. <br /> <br /> Not only that, but it is essential that all Inspired types work similarly because they are all part of the same game and system. Writing up different Facet types for each Inspired type is a lot of extra work when it still doesn't make them look anything like an actual nova or psiad. We put a lot of work into giving nods to the &quot;future&quot; game lines in what mesmerists and stalwarts might hint at, but they are not those things. <br /> <br /> Daredevils are capable of Dramatic Editing far easier than mesmerists and stalwarts because they are probability manipulators. This is why they have a discount to doing it. But all Inspired characters can manipulate Telluric Energy to get some dramatic effect. This is the nature of the pulp style of the game, and again, all characters need to feel like they are all part of the same game, so they all get to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444636#post1444636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest change is to make Dramatic Editing available to all player characters and major antagonists (but not extras), whether or not they're Inspired, through Momentum but not Inspiration; this would include stalwarts and mesmerists, and daredevils would remain the only characters who can spend Inspiration on traditional Dramatic Editing while stalwarts and mesmerists would still get their alternatives to it that they can spend their Inspiration on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this might sound like a good fix, but it actually makes Dramatic Editing *easier* for mesmerists and stalwarts. Momentum is a rather easy resources to generate and is intended to fill quickly so players are interested in using it often. Inspiration is less easy to come by, and the design behind it as a resource is to make players weigh their options on what to do in any given scene because it won't come back until the scene is over. We have lots of ways to get it back, but if you spend 3 in one scene, you aren't going to get any of it back until the scene ends. Momentum on the other hand might generate in the middle of the scene due to failed rolls. Meaning that it is actually easier to Dramatic Edit using Momentum rather than Inspiration, as the resource procs more often.<br /> <br /> Both of these resources are wholly out of character even if one describes a character's state. Momentum reflects the push and pull of winning and losing. The motivation someone gets when they get knocked down and stand back up to fight. Inspiration reflects the will someone exerts over the world around them. It's the lucky breaks, the force of mind, and the sheer audacity Inspired characters exhibit. Characters do not talk about Inspiration or Momentum. They do not know that either exists. They might talk about being mentally or physically drained, but they aren't going to say something like &quot;I'm out of Inspiration.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T09:36:27-07:00","id":1444838,"title":"","content":"Danielle, not questioning the design choices, but the way some terms are being used. I know you wrote Core and Adventure and all the others, just want to understand exactly what is what.<br /> <br /> Inspired is used in Core to describe anyone that has powers, it includes Novas, Psions and Psiads. So saying Stalwarts and Mesmerists are inspired is not really different from saying Novas and Psions are inspired.<br /> <br /> Ian (and I believe you too) said Stalwarts are low powered Novas and Mesmerists are low powered Psiads, that, as I understand, means if a Stalwart train a lot it\u2019s possible to become a full blown Nova. The changes in the system are more about putting everybody in the same level and same rule set than saying they are different. For example, if a Superior somehow were build in the adventure era they would be built as Stalwarts, and not following the superiors rules, the same way we use Aeon Aberrant rules to build Aberrants and not Aberrant Nova rules (ok now it was confusing, but I hope you get).<br /> <br /> From your last post I understand the opposite, Stalwarts are proto-Novas, the same way a Psiad is not a Psion and will never be unless something happen. I don\u2019t know if you are aware of a 1e unofficial source book called Awaiting Inspirations, that basically put Mesmerists and Stalwarts as variations of Daredevils instead of low powered Psiads and Novas, in TC terms, basically they would be Flux users that are really good in reaching the psi and quantum, but still handle only flux.<br /> <br /> My understanding reading last week manuscript is that Flux is so intense (the barrier between realities is so week) that even non-probability manipulators can handle some dramatic editing, and daredevils can DE so easily they don\u2019t spend Inspiration (they spend momentum) and recover inspiration by boldness, things that are not possible in later eras (or before Hammersmith) because the lower level of Flux (stronger barrier between realities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:00:11-07:00","id":1444844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444832#post1444832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's an assumption going on here that the mechanics are not supporting the fiction, and I think people are getting too caught up in the weeds about mesmerists and stalwarts being proto-versions of later iterations of novas and psions. Mesmerists and stalwarts are INSPIRED characters. They are not novas and psions. Not even &amp;quot;not yet.&amp;quot; They are Inspired just like Talents are. The reason the TC Core says that only Talents get Dramatic Editing is because they are the only Inspired type to make it out of the Inspired Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>That suggestion has been made by several of us, and has been shot down by Ian Watson: specifically, he has said that stalwarts and mesmerists are <i>not</i> offshoots of daredevils, and <i>are</i> \u201cproto-novas\u201d and \u201cproto-psiads\u201d. He has said that you're free to treat them as offshoots of daredevils in your game is that works for you, but that that's not the intent. <br /> <br /> I'd be fine if the official position were to change to what you're describing, by the way. But as it stands, the rules do support what you're describing while Ian's assertions don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444832#post1444832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only that, but it is essential that all Inspired types work similarly because they are all part of the same game and system. Writing up different Facet types for each Inspired type is a lot of extra work when it still doesn't make them look anything like an actual nova or psiad. We put a lot of work into giving nods to the &amp;quot;future&amp;quot; game lines in what mesmerists and stalwarts might hint at, but they are not those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I never proposed the \u201calternate Facets\u201d thing as an official change. It was a house-rule musing that I gave since realized was a mistake to even mention here, as people have taken it as an official suggestion even though I specifically said that it wasn't. That said, I'll keep your comments in mind when working out the details of this particular house rule. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444832#post1444832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daredevils are capable of Dramatic Editing far easier than mesmerists and stalwarts because they are probability manipulators. This is why they have a discount to doing it. But all Inspired characters can manipulate Telluric Energy to get some dramatic effect. This is the nature of the pulp style of the game, and again, all characters need to feel like they are all part of the same game, so they all get to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Not once have I suggested otherwise, and I have explicitly argued against that notion when it has come up.<br /> <br /> The only area where I disagree is that if Ian is right, then the telluric energies that the stalwarts and mesmerists wield are of the same sort that the later Novas and psiads wheeled, which explicitly can't be used for the sort of Dramatic Editing that daredevils do. Not \u201caren't as effective at it\u201d; but \u201ccan't do it\u201d. Though even if that's so, it doesn't mean that stalwarts and mesmerists shouldn't be able to do the daredevil style Dramatic Editing; it just means that a different rationale is needed. Which is where I'm coming from when I suggest reviving the first edition's notion that it's just a genre convention, for everyone that you want to engage in that sort of Dramatic Editing who isn't a daredevil. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444832#post1444832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this might sound like a good fix, but it actually makes Dramatic Editing *easier* for mesmerists and stalwarts. Momentum is a rather easy resources to generate and is intended to fill quickly so players are interested in using it often. Inspiration is less easy to come by, and the design behind it as a resource is to make players weigh their options on what to do in any given scene because it won't come back until the scene is over. We have lots of ways to get it back, but if you spend 3 in one scene, you aren't going to get any of it back until the scene ends. Momentum on the other hand might generate in the middle of the scene due to failed rolls. Meaning that it is actually easier to Dramatic Edit using Momentum rather than Inspiration, as the resource procs more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one reason I suggested going with non-daredevils paying double the normal cost in Momentum instead of the \u201c+1 Inspiration\u201d that the manuscript requires. If you feel that that's not enough, triple or quadruple it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444832#post1444832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of these resources are wholly out of character even if one describes a character's state. Momentum reflects the push and pull of winning and losing. The motivation someone gets when they get knocked down and stand back up to fight. Inspiration reflects the will someone exerts over the world around them. It's the lucky breaks, the force of mind, and the sheer audacity Inspired characters exhibit. Characters do not talk about Inspiration or Momentum. They do not know that either exists. They might talk about being mentally or physically drained, but they aren't going to say something like &amp;quot;I'm out of Inspiration.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But they <i>might</i> talk about it in the same way that Novas talk about quantum energies or psions and psiads talk about noetic energies. They do, after all, have the notion that telleric energies exist. And there are some that can even sense telluric energies, even if they can't make the distinction between what stalwarts and mesmerists wield, and can't sense what daredevils wield.<br /> <br /> Basically, it would help if I wasn't getting mixed messages from the developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:33:46-07:00","id":1444857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444844#post1444844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That suggestion has been made by several of us, and has been shot down by Ian Watson: specifically, he has said that stalwarts and mesmerists are <i>not</i> offshoots of daredevils, and <i>are</i> \u201cproto-novas\u201d and \u201cproto-psiads\u201d. He has said that you're free to treat them as offshoots of daredevils in your game is that works for you, but that that's not the intent.<br /> <br /> I'd be fine if the official position were to change to what you're describing, by the way. But as it stands, the rules do support what you're describing while Ian's assertions don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're conflating terms here.<br /> <br /> I said stalwarts and mesmerists are not offshoots of daredevils.<br /> <br /> Danielle is saying stalwarts, mesmerists, and daredevils are all Inspired characters.<br /> <br /> Neither of those statements disagree with each other. I think you're reading &quot;daredevil&quot; as &quot;Inspired&quot; or vice versa.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:46:53-07:00","id":1444861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444838#post1444838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ian (and I believe you too) said Stalwarts are low powered Novas and Mesmerists are low powered Psiads, that, as I understand, means if a Stalwart train a lot it\u2019s possible to become a full blown Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is a leap on your part that is not inherent in the statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:49:29-07:00","id":1444864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444857#post1444857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're conflating terms here.<br /> <br /> I said stalwarts and mesmerists are not offshoots of daredevils.<br /> <br /> Danielle is saying stalwarts, mesmerists, and daredevils are all Inspired characters.<br /> <br /> Neither of those statements disagree with each other. I think you're reading &amp;quot;daredevil&amp;quot; as &amp;quot;Inspired&amp;quot; or vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Because what Danielle just said sounds an awful lot like stalwarts and mesmerists being of the same sort of thing as talents, thus explaining their (limited) ability to use daredevil style Dramatic Editing. That is, it sounds like stalwarts being to Novas as QKs are to Novas: people who use what the core book calls Flux to manipulate what Aberrant calls Quantum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:35:32-07:00","id":1444876,"title":"","content":"I guess the problem is in part we don't have a distinct definition for &quot;Inspired&quot;, because the definition from the Core would seem to include Psiads and Novas, but Danielle is seeming to use it as a term that specifically includes all Dramatic Editors, but not non-Dramatic-Editing empowered people, which makes Mesmerists and Stalwarts Inspired at the same time that they are the evolutionary predecessors of Psiads and Novas, who not Inspired.... which would seem to back up my &quot;divergent evolution&quot; read (think off shoot subspecies whose descendents end up being completely separate species as their differences increase and similarities decrease), but this is likely not to be a topic the text will specifically nail down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:57:42-07:00","id":1444884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a person interacts with telluric energy particles, such as psi or quantum, they should become more inundated with the substance and grow in power. For some reason, the Doyen\u2019s energy barrier prevents the key level of interaction that would be necessary for an individual to become so powerful that they might go from an Inspired individual to a full psion or nova. </div> </div> </div>It sounds like the Doyen barrier is the thing preventing Stalwarts and Mesmerists to evolve into Novas and Psiads. Not sure if it would apply to the \u201ceruption\u201d or the further evolution with training,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-20-2021, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:00:52-07:00","id":1444885,"title":"","content":"<b>I may be more upfront</b> - but I simply think that in final <b>TC: Adventure</b>! version, some <b>simple frame describing 'gameline canon' on Inspired terms, Dramatic Editing, etc.</b> would be in order. It would only be one paragraph extra to write - but it would will solve whole confusion we have in this topic... And, let's be honest, this forum topic is read by <b>TC</b> nerds - normal players and STs will be <b>MUCH more confused on the whole issue</b>, if it will be left as it is in manuscript preview text.<br /> <br /> So I propose simple <i>Frame On This Subject</i> to be added to final <b>TC: Adventure</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We simply need official canon on this, up front, direct in text - that's all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-20-2021, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:11:50-07:00","id":1444890,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, Tesla is canonical expert on Strange Places - interesting use of historical figure... \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:13:42-07:00","id":1444892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444885#post1444885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]normal players and STs will be <b>MUCH more confused on the whole issue</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that &quot;normal&quot; STs and players will simply enjoy the book as written and won't care about the minutiae of the setting metaphysics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:15:28-07:00","id":1444893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444892#post1444892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect that &quot;normal&quot; STs and players will simply enjoy the book as written and won't care about the minutiae of the setting metaphysics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agree completely!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:25:07-07:00","id":1444897,"title":"","content":"To be clear I\u2019m fine with these questions not being answered in canon. Theorizing though gives fodder for at table hypotheses of Pandora, Tantalus, and Utopia PCs and NPCs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:50:16-07:00","id":1444900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444876#post1444876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the problem is in part we don't have a distinct definition for &quot;Inspired&quot;, because the definition from the Core would seem to include Psiads and Novas, but Danielle is seeming to use it as a term that specifically includes all Dramatic Editors, but not non-Dramatic-Editing empowered people, which makes Mesmerists and Stalwarts Inspired at the same time that they are the evolutionary predecessors of Psiads and Novas, who not Inspired.... which would seem to back up my &quot;divergent evolution&quot; read (think off shoot subspecies whose descendents end up being completely separate species as their differences increase and similarities decrease), but this is likely not to be a topic the text will specifically nail down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you please point to me where in the Core book that talks about Inspired characters that it seems to include psiads and novas? I'd honestly like to know because I have spent a lot of time trying to distinguish between powered character (all character types) and Inspired characters, the only ones of which show up in TC Core at Talents.<br /> <br /> You're right that the text isn't going to nail down the specific distinctions between mesmerists/psiad and stalwart/nova. But for the purposes of Adventure! (and not contradicted anywhere else as far as I'm aware), mesmerists and stalwarts are Inspired characters and operate under the same rule as all other Inspired characters. <br /> <br /> I have a long essay somewhere in the back of my brain about what telluric energy is and how it relates to quantum and psi particles and why mesmerists and stalwarts aren't just psiads and novas. Maybe one day I can be convinced to write it up and toss it into a blog post or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:58:12-07:00","id":1444903,"title":"","content":"Thinking this over some more: I don't mean to sound argumentative, but perhaps the confusion is coming from a conflation that you have done. What I keep on running into is the way Inspiration conflates four things: the three kinds of telluric energies (which I don't have a problem with) and \u201cit's just a genre convention; don't sweat the details!\u201d (which I do). <br /> <br /> First of all: are stalwarts using telluric energy to do the kinds of narrative adjustments that the core book describes, or is that \u201cjust a genre convention\u201d? I personally prefer the latter, and have been basing my arguments on that. But if it's the former, then another can of worms has been opened: specifically, stalwarts are doing something with telluric energy that Novas can't do with Quantum energy. And this implies that the telluric energies that stalwarts wield at least partially includes something like whatever it is that daredevils wield. That's where suggestions such as stalwarts being like QKs come from. Again, not my preference. But at least it makes sense.<br /> <br /> My preference is that it's just a genre convention for stalwarts. My fallback position is that it's a QK type of thing. But to say that they use telluric energy to alter the narrative and then imply that they don't? That's crossing wires. <br /> <br /> The Inspiration vs. Momentum thing is of secondary importance to this. I like the Momentum angle because there's no doubt about what Momentum is; and staying that stalwarts use Momentum leaves no confusion about any possibility that they're using telluric energies to shape the narrative (as opposed to using telluric energies to exceed their limits, which I don't have a problem with, but which I don't consider to be shaping the narrative; that's another conflation which I reject). But the important part is leaving no doubt to the reader that stalwart and mesmerist narrative changes are genre convention, not the result of telluric energy. (Again, that's option one. Option two pretty much requires the rules to remain as they are.}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:01:19-07:00","id":1444904,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the late response. I'm at work, and composing these messages when I have a few seconds to spare. So I didn't have a chance to read anything else going on before I posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:08:08-07:00","id":1444905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444900#post1444900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a long essay somewhere in the back of my brain about what telluric energy is and how it relates to quantum and psi particles and why mesmerists and stalwarts aren't just psiads and novas. Maybe one day I can be convinced to write it up and toss it into a blog post or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be immensely useful to include something to this effect in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:15:15-07:00","id":1444906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444905#post1444905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be immensely useful to include something to this effect in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the book as is I already interesting to newcomers and \u201cnormal players\u201d. BUT it would be an awesome introduction to the Addendum!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:21:22-07:00","id":1444907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444903#post1444903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking this over some more: I don't mean to sound argumentative, but perhaps the confusion is coming from a conflation that you have done. What I keep on running into is the way Inspiration conflates four things: the three kinds of telluric energies (which I don't have a problem with) and \u201cit's just a genre convention; don't sweat the details!\u201d (which I do).<br /> <br /> First of all: are stalwarts using telluric energy to do the kinds of narrative adjustments that the core book describes, or is that \u201cjust a genre convention\u201d? I personally prefer the latter, and have been basing my arguments on that. But if it's the former, then another can of worms has been opened: specifically, stalwarts are doing something with telluric energy that Novas can't do with Quantum energy. And this implies that the telluric energies that stalwarts wield at least partially includes something like whatever it is that daredevils wield. That's where suggestions such as stalwarts being like QKs come from. Again, not my preference. But at least it makes sense.<br /> <br /> My preference is that it's just a genre convention for stalwarts. My fallback position is that it's a QK type of thing. But to say that they use telluric energy to alter the narrative and then imply that they don't? That's crossing wires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so the answer here is that I'm not contradicting myself, both things are true. It is a genre convention that we wished to preserve from Adventure! 1e that all characters could dramatically edit. But there's also an in-setting answer as to why stalwarts and mesmerists can manipulate telluric energy in a way that novas and psiads absolutely cannot do in later years. Most of the science stuff about psi and quantum particles are pseudoscience, so this answer is equally unclean and wonky. But the simple answer is that the Doyen energy barrier's effects on those particles is so profound that it has fundamentally changed how those characters interact with their particles. To the point where if I were to make a character sheet for Dr. Primoris and Sara Kaur in Adventure! I would use the stalwart and mesmerist templates because they cannot express the later templates with the energy barrier in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:27:22-07:00","id":1444908,"title":"","content":"So the alterations remain in effect all the way up to the point where Divas Mal shatters the Doyen barrier. I can buy that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:31:33-07:00","id":1444909,"title":"","content":"That is a great answer answer that close this issue very well!<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot, Danielle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}